    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Chosen for what it is NOT. The obvious neighbouring import, `Nat.not_succ_le_zero`, was dropped from this set after checking rather than assuming: our own Nat prelude already proves it, axiom-free, on the `kernel-lean` route (`nat_theorem_inventory` and `theorem_axiom_footprint`, measured 2026-08-15). Landing an imported fact for a proposition we had already constructed a proof of would have understated what this project holds -- and it would have made the ledger's route counts read as though the import were the only evidence.\n\nNote the two are NOT the same formal statement even though they are the same mathematics: ours is stated over the kernel's own `Nat.le`, Lean's goes through the `LE` type class as `LE.le.{0} Nat instLENat`. That gap between `same proposition` and `same statement` is the alignment problem `02-synthesize.md` describes, arriving concretely on the first five imports. `Nat.le_succ` itself is absent from our prelude, so no such collision arises here.",
        "type": "prose"
